<name>Brake</name>
<section id="1002J_S000U" variety="S000U">
<name>Brake Control</name>
<ttl id="1002J_S000U_744TG_T0089" variety="T0089">
<name>ABS with EBD &amp; TRC &amp; VSC &amp; BA System</name>
<para id="RM000000NC000IX" category="C" type-id="300F5" name-id="442OL-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>C1232/32</dtccode>
<dtcname>G Sensor Stuck Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1234/34</dtccode>
<dtcname>Yaw Rate Sensor Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1243/43</dtccode>
<dtcname>G Sensor Stuck Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1244/44</dtccode>
<dtcname>G Sensor Open or Short</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1245/45</dtccode>
<dtcname>G Sensor Output Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000NC000IX_05" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007O400000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The skid control computer (built into the actuator) receives the yaw rate sensor signals via CAN communication.</ptxt>
<ptxt>The yaw rate sensor has a built-in G sensor.</ptxt>
<ptxt>If there is a malfunction in the communication line with the yaw rate sensor, DTCs "U0123/62 (yaw rate sensor communication malfunction)" and "U0124/95 (G sensor communication malfunction)" are output.</ptxt>
<ptxt>If a CAN communication line malfunction code is output, perform troubleshooting for the CAN communication line malfunction first.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.50in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.81in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.77in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Output Related Items</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1232/32</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>At a vehicle speed of 10km/h or more, a condition in which either GL1 or GL2 does not change continues for 30 seconds or more</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Yaw rate sensor (G sensor internally stuck)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1234/34</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A sensor malfunction signal is received from the yaw rate sensor when the IG1 terminal voltage is 9.5to17.4V</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw rate sensor improperly installed</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw Rate Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1243/43</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A condition in which the values of GL1 and GL2 both do not change by 0.0294G or more while the vehicle speed goes from 30km/h to 0km/h occurs 16 times or more</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Yaw rate sensor (G sensor internally stuck)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1244/44</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>A data malfunction signal is received from the G sensor when the IG1 terminal voltage is 9.5to17.4V</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>With the vehicle stopped, after the difference between GL1 and GL2 becomes 0.6G or more, it does not become less than 0.4G for 60 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Yaw rate sensor (G sensor)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1245/45</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>At a vehicle speed of 30km/h or more, the difference between the longitudinal G calculated from the G sensor value and the longitudinal G calculated from the vehicle speed exceeds 0.35G for 60 seconds or more</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw rate sensor improperly installed</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw Rate Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
